<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Datasets Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Training Dataset</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We organize our training data into three categories based on the memory capabilities they target, as illustrated in Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Training Dataset Preparation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Mem-𝛼: Learning Memory Construction via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. The detailed dataset statistics are provided in Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ A.1 Training Dataset ‣ Appendix A Datasets Details ‣ Mem-𝛼: Learning Memory Construction via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
