<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Additional Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mem-𝛼: Learning Memory Construction via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, we show the performance comparison of different <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> on the validation dataset. We also compare these settings on the test dataset (MemoryAgentBench), shown in Table <a href="#A3.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ C.4 Additional Ablation Study ‣ Appendix C Experimental Details ‣ Mem-𝛼: Learning Memory Construction via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. The observations are consistent with Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mem-𝛼: Learning Memory Construction via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
